   "text": "## Step 13\n\nBack to the best config (41.75%). With step 15 as a guaranteed fallback to this known-good config, I can afford to **experiment** in steps 13\u201314.\n\nThe single largest error is **1\u21927 (518)**. A \"1\" matches the `7` template via the shared central/diagonal stroke. The cleanest distinguisher: a real `7` has essentially no ink at the **bottom row**, whereas a `1` has a base serif there. So I add a *tiny, targeted* mild anti-region (\u22120.3) only at the bottom cells where `1`'s base sits but `7` doesn't (keeping `7`'s own diagonal foot intact). Everything else stays exactly at the step-10 optimum, so the effect is isolated.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# '#' = +1 ink, 'x' = -0.3 mild anti-region, '.' = 0\nTEMPLATES = {\n    0: [\"............\",\"...#####....\",\"..##...##...\",\"..#.....#...\",\"..#.....#...\",\n        \"..#.....#...\",\"..#.....#...\",\"..#.....#...\",\"..##...##...\",\"...#####....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    1: [\"............\",\".....##.....\",\"....###.....\",\"...#.##.....\",\".....##.....\",\n        \".....##.....\",\".....##.....\",\".....##.....\",\".....##.....\",\"...######...\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    2: [\"............\",\"...#####....\",\"..##...##...\",\".......##...\",\"......##....\",\n        \".....##.....\",\"....##......\",\"...##.......\",\"..##........\",\"..########..\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    3: [\"............\",\"..######....\",\".......##...\",\".......##...\",\"....###.....\",\n        \"....###.....\",\".......##...\",\".......##...\",\"..##...##...\",\"...#####....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    4: [\"............\",\".....###....\",\"....#.##....\",\"...#..##....\",\"..#...##....\",\n        \"..########..\",\"......##....\",\"......##....\",\"......##....\",\"......##....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    5: [\"............\",\"..#######...\",\"..##........\",\"..##........\",\"..#####.....\",\n        \".......##...\",\".......##...\",\".......##...\",\"..##..##....\",\"...####.....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    6: [\"............\",\"....####....\",\"...##.......\",\"..##........\",\"..##........\",\n        \"..######....\",\"..##...##...\",\"..#.....#...\",\"..##...##...\",\"...#####....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    # 7: added mild negatives at bottom-right where 1's base serif lies (keeps 7's own foot at col4,5)\n    7: [\"............\",\"..########..\",\".......##...\",\"......##....\",\"......##....\",\n        \".....##.....\",\".....##.....\",\"....##......\",\"....##......\",\"...x##xxx...\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    8: [\"............\",\"...#####....\",\"..##...##...\",\"..##...##...\",\"...#####....\",\n        \"...#####....\",\"..##...##...\",\"..##...##...\",\"..##...##...\",\"...#####....\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n    9: [\"............\",\"...#####....\",\"..##...##...\",\"..#.....#...\",\"..##...##...\",\n        \"...######...\",\".......##...\",\"......##....\",\".....##.....\",\"...###......\",\n        \"............\",\"............\"],\n}\n\nBIAS = np.array([0.89, -0.17, 0.78, 0.63, -0.34, 0.92, 0.28, 0.25, -0.30, 0.09],\n                dtype=np.float32)\n\n\ndef _val(ch):\n    return 1.0 if ch == '#' else (-0.3 if ch == 'x' else 0.0)\n\n\ndef build_weights():\n    scale = 2.0\n\n    conv1_w = np.zeros((8, 1, 5, 5), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k in range(8):\n        conv1_w[k, 0, 2, 2] = 1.0\n    conv1_b = np.zeros((8,), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    conv2_w = np.zeros((16, 8, 5, 5), dtype=np.float32)\n    for c in range(16):\n        conv2_w[c, 0, c // 4, c % 4] = 1.0\n    conv2_b = np.zeros((16,), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    T = {}\n    for d, rows in TEMPLATES.items():\n        g = np.array([[_val(ch) for ch in r] for r in rows], dtype=np.float32)\n        g = g - g.mean()\n        n = np.linalg.norm(g)\n        T[d] = g / n if n > 0 else g\n\n    cnt = np.zeros((12, 12), dtype=np.float32)\n    for c in range(16):\n        ro, co = c // 4, c % 4\n        for u in range(4):\n            for v in range(4):\n                cnt[min(ro + 2 * u, 11), min(co + 2 * v, 11)] += 1.0\n    cnt[cnt == 0] = 1.0\n\n    fc_w = np.zeros((10, 256), dtype=np.float32)\n    for d in range(10):\n        for c in range(16):\n            ro, co = c // 4, c % 4\n            for u in range(4):\n                for v in range(4):\n                    idx = c * 16 + u * 4 + v\n                    r = min(ro + 2 * u, 11)\n                    col = min(co + 2 * v, 11)\n                    fc_w[d, idx] = scale * T[d][r, col] / cnt[r, col]\n\n    fc_b = BIAS.copy()\n\n    return {\n        \"conv1.weight\": conv1_w, \"conv1.bias\": conv1_b,\n        \"conv2.weight\": conv2_w, \"conv2.bias\": conv2_b,\n        \"fc.weight\": fc_w, \"fc.bias\": fc_b,\n    }\n```",
